+# Scope and method
+
+Static review on 2026-10-17 of main at
+`229ce38535142958ab75aa1b0462d8be37dbf77e`, after #964 and dependency update
+#965 merged. Three independent domain reviews covered analyzer/target/plan/review,
+execution/resource/workspace/metrics, and persistence/configuration/Python tooling.
+The coordinator traced core state, budget accounting and disk lifecycle, then
+independently checked both proposed changes. No runtime tests, implementation
+builds, benchmarks or Lean proof/compiler runs were performed for this audit.
+
+The criterion from software-design-philosophy is fewer maintained decisions,
+representations or caller obligations. Backward compatibility is not required.
+A current error boundary, platform capability or historical observation still
+needs its own justification before deletion. Previous audits supplied questions,
+not current evidence. Inspection covered declarations, current writers/readers,
+failure paths and selected test assertions; it was not a line-by-line review of
+all mutation operators or every OS implementation.
+
+The reviewed worktree is isolated on `audit/2026-10-17-post964`. The original
+working tree and its user files were left unchanged. Open Issues #743, #806 and
+#570 were checked; there were no open PRs at the start. #743 remains deferred
+pending concrete demand for another language, so this audit does not restart a
+generic plugin or language-separation project.
+
+# Assessment
+
+**7.5/10: six of eight diagnostic rows evidenced for the inspected boundaries.**
+This qualitative score is not a repository-wide correctness measure. The new
+Windows finding exposes a misleading ownership representation that earlier
+reviews did not identify; the lower score does not imply #964 introduced it.
+
+| Diagnostic | Result | Evidence or required action |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| Module purposes are describable | Pass | Core decides transitions; shell executes effects; analyzer, workspace and persistence have distinct responsibilities. |
+| Interfaces are simpler than implementations | Pass | Typed requests, validated plans and managed ownership hide substantial implementation work. |
+| Implementation rules can change locally | Pass | Both new proposals stay inside their owning modules; shared candidate/report validation already has owners. Test/fuzz source inclusion remains layout coupling, not a new production policy split. |
+| Interface comments describe abstractions | Pass | Process cancellation, spool transfer and cleanup contracts explain lifetime and evidence limits. |
+| Design discussion occurs in review | Pass | Current maintenance records and this alternatives review record invariants and rejected simplifications. |
+| Modules hide important decisions | Pass | Transition, budget, storage, measurement and OS cleanup decisions have established owners. |
+| A newcomer can understand boundaries without reading implementations | Needs work | RootSignal suggests live violation propagation that never occurs; the copied plan allowance suggests a second meaningful amount. Resolve #966/#967 and document actual ownership. |
+| 10–20% actual design-time allocation | Unmeasured | No time-allocation evidence was collected. Measure the investment before awarding this row. |
+
+An evidenced 10/10 requires both the bounded ownership clarification and evidence
+for the investment criterion. Additional nominal enums would not supply either.
+
+# Finding 1: retain only the bound copy reservation ID
+
+[Issue #966](https://github.com/HayaoSuzuki/hoimin/issues/966), low priority.
+`PlanState.reservation` stores `(ReservationId, u64)`. Before binding, its sole
+production writer checks the request allowance against the immutable plan's
+`aggregate_bytes`; validation later compares that same request with the stored
+amount again. Plan clones retain the same aggregate and share the state. Thus
+this second comparison cannot reject an otherwise valid request through current
+production construction. `reservation_id()` only projects the ID. Replace the
+tuple with `Option<ReservationId>` and remove the duplicate comparison.
+[^post964-copy]
+
+Keep preflight/range/aggregate/reservation validation order, including zero
+allowance. Preserve initial binding, worker-slot admission and grant publication
+under their existing lock. Materialization failure releases the slot and partial
+charge but keeps the reservation bound. `CopyAllowance.granted/charged` remains
+necessary for publication and concurrent accounting; it is outside the deletion.
+The private copy module and private plan fields expose no external path that
+forges a different stored allowance.[^post964-copy]
+
+The Issue requests finite rejection/precedence tables and bounded generated
+requests against a fixed plan aggregate, with independent expected acceptance.
+Existing atomic binding, grant publication, failed-copy retry, worker-drop and
+accounting tests remain obligations. New Lean models are unnecessary if transition
+semantics remain unchanged; existing relevant correspondence tests should run.
+This audit establishes redundant representation, not a reproduced runtime bug.
+
+# Finding 2: remove the inert Windows violation carrier
+
+[Issue #967](https://github.com/HayaoSuzuki/hoimin/issues/967), low priority.
+`RootSignal.violations` has no writer after zero initialization. Run-wide
+`mark_active` is a no-op because memory/process limits live on nested root jobs.
+Yet `WindowsSupervisor` owns an Arc of this value and passes it through root
+registration and classification. `ActiveRoot.signal` stores a Weak that is never
+upgraded: only its presence is observed. It represents interest in receiving an
+exit notification, not shared violation state or observed liveness.
+[^post964-windows]
+
+Remove the zero-only carrier, its parameter plumbing and dead outer
+classification. Represent exit-notification interest directly with a documented
+bool or small enum. Preserve UUID/PID generation, retained process handles,
+notification-consumed versus process-signaled barriers, timeout behavior, and
+mutex release while waiting. Confirm actual job emptiness before processing
+ACTIVE_PROCESS_ZERO, and publish only interested roots. Detached generations must
+remain until their exit evidence is consumed; removing interest does not justify
+removing the registry entry.[^post964-windows]
+
+The real nested-job completion-port classifier remains, including memory-limit
+precedence when both violation kinds are observed. Do not restore run-wide
+attribution to sibling workers: that was the separately resolved bug
+[#340](https://github.com/HayaoSuzuki/hoimin/issues/340). AtomicU8 and Ordering still
+have test-only close-failure uses; process-handle Arcs have independent lifetime
+roles. The Issue requires native Windows checks for attach failures, delayed
+notifications, retained generations, handle waits and nested limits. Other-host
+builds or static inspection cannot substitute for those executions.
+[^post964-windows]
+
+# Other candidates examined
+
+| Candidate | Decision and counterexample |
+| --- | --- |
+| Disk statistics latest/global cache | #964 already removed them. The retained-history accessor preserves the established monitor boundary; do not reopen #963. |
+| Pending completion metadata and core flags | Worker identity, cleanup reservations and output continuations serve different completion validation. Attempts, outcome history and report progress are not mutually exclusive phases. No replacement demonstrated fewer maintained rules. [^post964-machine] |
+| Analysis diagnostic queue and deferred result | One producer transfers diagnostics out of its result, and one continuation consumes the queue then applies the result. Bundling this private pair is possible but did not remove repeated policy. [^post964-machine] |
+| Budget active/released/frontier | They support accounting, duplicate-release diagnostics and ID exhaustion. Deriving release history from dense allocation couples new invariants for no demonstrated current benefit. [^post964-budget] |
+| Disk lifecycle secondary history | Historical errors may exist before a primary stop; snapshot enrichment is a projection, not two independently updated primary histories. Cleanup and drain evidence cannot be inferred from task counts. [^post964-disk] |
+| Process start gate and cancellation | Synchronization algorithms resemble each other, but admission stopping and process termination have independent identities. A helper with wrappers adds pass-through interfaces; no current divergent rule or meaningful net gain was established. [^post964-process] |
+| Shell counters, cleanup and end-observation state | Completion-channel receipt and task join are separate events. An attempted end measurement can fail, so absent data does not mean unattempted. Retain these independent facts. [^post964-shell] |
+| Analyzer prefix, control flow and spool state | Prefix overflow survives eviction; several abrupt exit categories can coexist. Planning returns candidates while runtime transfers a spool with a different cleanup lifetime. Typed operators and shared projection already centralize names/validation. [^post964-analyzer][^post964-analyzer-handler] |
+| Target DiffPlan::Legacy | This is a live fallback for rename/copy/unmerged entries and long pathspecs, not old-format support. Removing it changes rename pairing or current bounded discovery behavior. [^post964-target] |
+| Ranked selection and saved plan metadata | One normalized Top request and checked selection feed execution and preview. Source records include files producing no candidates; candidate hashes cannot replace them. [^post964-plan] |
+| Persisted session finished versus complete | Incomplete finalization and abrupt ownership loss are distinct history. Current schema rejection and row validation detect invalid saved input; they are not repair/migration compatibility. [^post964-session] |
+| Raw configuration and all_legacy | Raw intent normalizes once to SessionMode. The operator cohort has live default/fuzz callers; renaming or inlining it only relocates membership knowledge. [^post964-config] |
+| Report DTOs and optional fields | Progress and review have different current configuration needs; shared structural validation handles both. Narrowing internal event types would add wire/projection layers without a demonstrated reduction. Optional current-mode fields are not legacy adapters. [^post964-report-reader] |
+| Release wrappers, entry modes and retries | Typed expected failures serve live exception-based callers. Direct-script/module invocation, Windows text normalization and bounded publication visibility have current callers and environments. No obsolete compatibility layer justified deletion. [^post964-release][^post964-provenance] |
+
+# Review and publication
+
+Each domain report recorded five concrete passes. The coordinator performed
+these additional reviews and independent challenges before publication:
+
+| Stage | Five passes and results |
+| --- | --- |
+| Investigation | 1: pinned fetched main and merged PRs; 2: searched current declarations/writers/readers; 3: separated independent observations from exclusive states; 4: traced failure/timeout/concurrent ownership counterexamples; 5: compared simpler alternatives and rejected extra abstraction without net gain. |
+| Proposals | 1: confirmed immutable aggregate and sole reservation writer; 2: checked clone visibility/rollback/grant publication; 3: searched all Windows signal references and preserved real nested classification; 4: independently challenged handle waits, notification interest and generation retention; 5: reviewed both Japanese drafts, adding fixed-plan property expectations, valid-request competition and explicit wait/empty-job safeguards. |
+| Publication | 1: checked open Issues/PRs; 2: searched all Issue states for PlanState, RootSignal, mark_active and reservation/allowance; 3: read resolved #340 and pinned source links; 4: created #966/#967 from reviewed drafts and checked their bodies; 5: checked this knowledge page's structure, source metadata, links and site rendering. |
+
+Publication readback confirmed both Issues OPEN with bodies matching the reviewed
+local drafts. Documentation verification on 2026-10-17 passed: 50 knowledge pages
+for structure, local links and reachability; changed-page source IDs/footnotes
+and all 16 recorded source hashes; strict site generation with
+`python -m tools.docs_site --output site`; and `git diff --check`. These checks
+validate documentation, not implementation behavior. A final independent read-only
+review of the Issue drafts and this audit found no material inconsistency.
+
+# Limits and recheck triggers
+
+This is static evidence, not a claim of fresh runtime, Windows, concurrency,
+performance or proof success. New test requirements in the Issues are future
+implementation obligations. In particular, the #963 implementation's passing
+tests were not rerun as part of this audit and are not current-audit results.
+Recheck if plan aggregate mutability, reservation writers, Windows notification
+producers, job limit placement or generation-retention rules change. Existing
+#743 remains a conditional broader design topic rather than a prerequisite for
+these two local reductions.
+
